  },
  "question": {
    "text": "The number of elements in the set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>{</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8469;</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>100</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math> is a multiple of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>}</mo></math>&nbsp;is _______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "15",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>N</mi></math>.</p><p>Let us take the values of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;and check whether&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;is divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;or not.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;is not divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;is not divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></math>&nbsp;is divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math></p><p>Similarly&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>13</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>13</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>&#946;</mi></math>&nbsp;is divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math></p><p>If we observe the pattern for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>13</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;is divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>.</p><p>That means the series forms an AP with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>.</p><p>Also&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>The required progression is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>But&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>100</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>N</mi></math></p><p>Therefore, the required answer is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math>.</p></blockquote>"
  }
}